{"repositoryId":90992283,"availability":"available","full":"zjuasmn/sketch-react","name":"sketch-react","description":"render sketch(v43+) file as react component","category":"Developer tools","language":"JavaScript","stars":98,"forks":11,"created":"2017-05-11T15:03:01Z","updated":"2018-04-04T02:34:07Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":"https://zjuasmn.github.io/sketch-react","topics":["developer-tools","react","shape","sketch"],"demo":"https://zjuasmn.github.io/sketch-react","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T13:37:56.873Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-12T13:37:56.873Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-12T13:37:56.873Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-12T13:37:56.873Z","stars":98,"forks":11}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Project is still in beta, help and advise are welcome.","The goal of this project is trying to reduce the gap between UI design and front-end development \\(for now, just html\\). A lot of time of front-end development is spent in matching the given UI design instead of implementing application logic. There are collaboration tools like Zeplin to help marking the design, but programmer still needs to measure and copy css for each element assemble them and copy icons and other assets one by one.","Here, we take a step further by generate html from .sketch file\\(v43+\\). So you can copy a group of element as html code and paste it in online or local text editor. Just a copy and paste from design to working code. Enjoy it."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/zjuasmn/sketch-react/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"2a93e70882eb406a50f1a8539dbd1b9d26afde55eace19805bd20c7cdbf108ec","extractedAt":"2026-10-12T13:37:57.055Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T13:37:57.055Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Project is still in beta, help and advise are welcome.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/zjuasmn/sketch-react/blob/master/README.md"},"audience":[],"r